WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:09.040
Speaker 1: yesterday or late the day before. A 12&nbsp;
page letter was released to the media, supposedly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:15.600
written by Donald Trump, weighing in on the Trump&nbsp;
riot committee hearings. Now, I don't believe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:20.960
for a second that Donald Trump really wrote a&nbsp;
12 page letter. Trump doesn't write and Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:28.960
doesn't read all he's capable of. As far as we've&nbsp;
seen is a tweet style messages, often with strange&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:33.600
grammar, spelling and syntax. So I don't believe&nbsp;
Trump wrote a 12 page letter. But I do believe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:39.200
that Trump sat somewhere and told someone what&nbsp;
to write. And Chris Cillizza from CNN received&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:45.840
the letter and gave us a list of the wackiest&nbsp;
things. And here are some some key, key moments&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:51.120
from this statement that shows us how the right&nbsp;
is thinking of these hearings. Number one, if they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:56.240
had any real evidence, they'd hold real hearings&nbsp;
with equal representation. Remember, Republicans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.240 --> 00:01:01.360
opted out of that. There was a framework for an&nbsp;
actual bipartisan committee ten members, five&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:06.800
Republicans, five Democrats, Democratic chair,&nbsp;
Republican vice chair, and both the chair and vice&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:12.160
chair have to agree on every subpoena. Republicans&nbsp;
rejected it. So Democrats did what they could,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:18.160
which is they've got Liz Cheney and Adam Kinzinger&nbsp;
on the panel so that that's their fault. Two, they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:23.520
use the illegally constituted committee to put on&nbsp;
a smoke and mirrors show for the American people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:28.240
in a pitiful last ditch effort to deceive the&nbsp;
American public again. There's nothing illegal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:33.760
about the committee. Just nothing. We've had other&nbsp;
committees, the Benghazi one. We've had others&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:39.040
perfectly legal. Number three, they've refused to&nbsp;
allow their political opponents to participate in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:44.160
the process. They've excluded exculpatory&nbsp;
witnesses and anyone who so easily points&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:51.360
out the flaws in their story. Again, as Chris&nbsp;
Cillizza writes, Republicans crushed the actual&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:56.880
bipartisan committee that they wanted to do,&nbsp;
that it is because of Republicans that they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:03.360
don't have more Republicans on the committee.&nbsp;
And also a whole bunch of the pro-Trump people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:08.080
that were subpoenaed didn't go. And that's now the&nbsp;
subject of legislation that includes Steve Bannon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:14.400
and Peter Navarro. Navarro for the unselected&nbsp;
pseudo committee, has coordinated with their media&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:20.400
puppets to broadcast their witnesses on TV without&nbsp;
opposition cross-examination or rebuttal evidence.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:26.480
Again, more than a thousand depositions were taken&nbsp;
of all sorts of witnesses. It is untrue that that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:32.240
is what was done. And then a whole bunch of other&nbsp;
just repetition of lies. I won't look at all of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:38.160
these, but number seven is they illegally&nbsp;
inflated voter rolls. That's unproven. They&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:43.547
illegally allowed harvested and stuffed ballots.&nbsp;
No evidence of that. They abused the use of mail&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.547 --> 00:02:48.000
in ballots. That's there's no evidence of that.&nbsp;
They physically removed Republicans from counting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:54.160
facilities. That's untrue. Now, there are random&nbsp;
Republicans who showed up demanding to oversee the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:59.200
election who were not allowed to because there's&nbsp;
a process for establishing observers there. There&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:03.840
were Republican and Democratic observers. There&nbsp;
were people who just showed up demanding access.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:11.440
It's sort of like if I go, you know, if I go to a&nbsp;
court and I say I want to sit alongside the judge,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:17.200
they would say, well, no, you haven't been&nbsp;
selected. You're not the judge. In the same way.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:22.160
If I'm not actually an election observer, I don't&nbsp;
have a right to just show up and be given power&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:28.880
there. But there is no evidence for any of those&nbsp;
claims and a whole bunch of other stuff that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:33.200
doesn't really have any meaning. Like Donald&nbsp;
Trump writing in this letter on election night,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:38.240
America watched as my lead grew and grew over&nbsp;
Biden as I was set to claim another victory.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:44.160
We expected the red mirage. We expected that&nbsp;
the early vote would favor Trump and that as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:48.880
the cities were counted overnight and into the&nbsp;
next day, it would start to point more in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:55.680
direction of Joe Biden. All of these things we&nbsp;
expected. So I don't believe Trump wrote this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.680 --> 00:04:02.400
but I do believe he had input. And it really shows&nbsp;
us that they aren't changing their talking points.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:08.640
Every day that passes, we have more of an&nbsp;
empirical basis to reject their claims,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:13.600
but they continue making the exact same&nbsp;
claims day after day after day. Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:18.320
at the end of the day, I don't know that these&nbsp;
hearings are really going to have any impact.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:23.440
They're getting an okay audience. My guess is the&nbsp;
people watching are mostly the people who already&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:27.360
don't believe the things that Donald Trump has&nbsp;
been saying. So whether these hearings will have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:34.000
any impact whatsoever remains to be seen. But the&nbsp;
the lies that they are telling continue to be the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:39.520
exact same lies. And at this point, I don't know&nbsp;
who's falling for them. We'll have more on this on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:44.400
our Instagram, which you can find at David Pakman&nbsp;
show. We'll be back right after this short break.

